## UI Improvements

Improved the interface so results are presented as business information instead of raw developer JSON.

Examples:

- FAQ answers are displayed as readable answer cards.
- Leads are displayed in a structured table.
- Follow-up messages are displayed as readable draft messages.
- Selected tool and status are displayed separately.
- Light background and readable text improve visibility.
- Safety information is clearly displayed.

## Safety Practice

Confirmed:

- Maximum tool calls: 3
- Follow-up action is draft-only.
- No automatic message sending.
- No automatic deletion.
- No automatic business-record updates.
- Tool failures are reported clearly.

## What I Learned

MCP provides a standard interface for connecting AI applications with tools and resources.

Python functions still contain the actual business logic.

The MCP server exposes selected capabilities so compatible AI applications can discover and use them.

I also learned that a good AI application needs both a reliable backend and a clear user interface.

